  "source_assessment": [
    "Fallible context, ECH acceptor and endpoint address preparation precedes TCP spawn. Raw handles are synchronously adopted into concrete ConnectionPeer before any further await; final async finish owns guarded fields even when unpolled.",
    "JoinSet owns accepted TCP workers immediately. The serving body and literal response remain unchanged. Completed joined outcomes are accumulated, with no early error return from collection.",
    "Stop closes listener before abort/drain. Only cancelled results whose IDs were unfinished at the owner's explicit cancellation snapshot are ignored; already-completed cancellation and panic errors remain typed. External cancellation racing the owner's request is not independently attributable.",
    "Count and QUIC primary errors still reach the bounded TCP join. Both stop signals precede QUIC result observation; finish_with_cleanup preserves exact single errors and concrete simultaneous primary/cleanup objects.",
    "ConnectionPeer Drop requests parent abort; dropping the TCP future drops its JoinSet and requests child abort. Neither Drop is an asynchronous join or synchronous destruction promise.",
    "Tokio1.53.1 actual join_next_with_id output, cancellation safety, ID methods, abort_all and Drop contracts match the implementation. Await/is_finished completion includes task destructor completion."
  ],
